{"author":{"id":"40e3ba2788b3b9fc163c354afc44e5f9d225bcf0a27e679aaa878dd6135c6dcb"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1777964244,"nonce":"0BhCaHXohHdjR5kuPgUd6PdnLUU=","message":"M2-3 shipped on main:\n\n- read_header(): on first call, slurps the archive into memory through __archive_read_ahead/__archive_read_consume, opens libuc2 against the slurped buffer, walks uc2_read_cdir to cache every entry (with uc2_get_tag for tagged entries).  Each subsequent call yields one entry mapped onto archive_entry_set_pathname/set_size/set_mtime/set_filetype/set_perm.\n- read_data(): runs uc2_extract through a buffering write callback (extract_buf), yields the entire decompressed entry in one slice, then ARCHIVE_EOF on next call.\n- read_data_skip + cleanup: correct.\n\nMemory model: archive is slurped fully on first read_header, so memory scales with archive size.  Acceptable for v1; seekable adapter via __archive_read_seek is a future revision.\n\nBuild verified: libuc2_libarchive.a compiles clean against libarchive 3.7.7 sources, exports archive_read_support_format_uc2, has expected undefined refs (__archive_check_magic, __archive_read_ahead, __archive_read_register_format, __archive_read_consume).\n\nRuntime end-to-end test against bsdtar requires building a custom libarchive that includes our plugin (the read-format API is internal -- system libarchive.so does not expose __archive_read_register_format).  Integration recipe documented in contrib/libarchive/README.md.  Automated bsdtar round-trip test is M7 in the original b0b06a5 milestone list and stays open as a separate follow-up.\n\nClosing this issue.","files":null}]}